FastWAM Q-Planning / DINOv3 adaptation

Algorithm and reference implementation:
  Beyond Imitation: Self-Improving Robot Policies via Off-Policy Q-Planning
  Varun Giridhar, Anant Khandelwal, Jeremy A. Collins, Ignat Georgiev, Animesh Garg
  arXiv:2608.21204v1
  https://github.com/varungiridhar/qplanning-code
  inspected commit: 4b955b42308e42bc0187b0a3c529c15b10f98447
  model source: varungiridhar/lerobot, tag qplanning-release-v1
  src/lerobot/policies/q_function/modeling_q_function.py
  Reference repository license: Apache-2.0.

This is a repository-native adaptation, not a bit-for-bit reproduction of the
paper: DINOv3 replaces DINOv2; PyTorch SDPA and activation checkpointing reduce
memory; padded action/text tokens are masked; the existing LeRobot FastWAM
video-cache path is reused for batched proposal generation. No upstream gate,
general environment launcher, actor-training method, or vendored model is added.

DINOv3 and T5 are loaded through Transformers. DINOv3 weights remain subject to
Meta's DINOv3 license; no weights or Meta source code are included here.
The existing repository's Apache-2.0 license applies to this integration.
